                <pb facs="0479" n="399" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg399"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">863.51 Relief Credits/222: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Edge</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-05-02T16:00:00+01:00">May 2, 1930—4 p.m.</date><lb/>[Received
                        May 2—1 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>126. Department’s 93, April 15, 6 p.m., to London. The French Government states
                    that the terms of the letter of April 16 last from Leith-Ross to the Austrian
                    Minister at London express the conditions to which it especially has
                    subordinated its adhesion to the emission of the Austrian loan.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edge</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
